'''
Poly Morphism ( many forms): 
- function / method behaviour inside the class 
there are two types of poly morphism we can observe in python
1. Run Time Poly morphism -> function/method is decided during run time 
- this is observed in inheritence 
- parent and child will have function with same name 
- but the child will redefine the implementation
2. Compile Time Poly morphism (rarely in python) -> decided during compiling 
- same class 

how python finds object properties or methods: 
1. first it search locally i.e, within the class 
if found it will return the  value or execute the function 
if not found it will move up in the inheritence chain 
2. if the parent and child don't have the property / method 
you will get error 
'''
# Run time Polymorphism / method overriding 
class Parent: 
    def display(self): 
        print("I'm in Parent")
class Child(Parent): 
    def display(self): 
        print("I'm in Child")
c = Child()
c.display()
# c.print() error as print is not their
p = Parent()
p.display()
